<BaseLayout title="Archive — Skyhook Industries" description="Historical Skyhook Industries concepts preserved for project context but no longer presented as the current development roadmap.">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Archive</p><h1>Early concepts, preserved in context.</h1><p>Skyhook Industries has explored ideas beyond the present tether program. Some were intentionally speculative; others used assumptions or schedules that no longer represent the project.</p></section>
    <section class="page-section prose"><div class="archive-note"><strong>Archive policy:</strong> material listed here is historical. It should not be interpreted as an active mission commitment, current engineering specification or current development schedule.</div><h2>Comet mission concepts</h2><p>The former website proposed using robotic infrastructure and in-situ resources to substantially alter the orbit of comet 26P/Grigg–Skjellerup. That concept is not part of the current Skyhook Industries development roadmap.</p><h2>Original Skyhook schedule</h2><p>The former site published prototype milestones beginning in 2024 and extending to a 4,252 km operational system in 2042. Those dates are retired. The current roadmap is risk-driven and advances through engineering gates rather than unsupported calendar commitments.</p><h2>Why preserve these?</h2><p>Deleting old thinking makes projects look cleaner than they really are. Preserving it with explicit status makes the evolution of the engineering visible without confusing old exploration with present claims.</p></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
